We loop over each number in the array, add it to the sum, and finally, we return the mean by dividing the sum by the length of the array. We make sure to cast 'sum' or 'numbers.length' to double before the division to get a precise result. If we don't do this, since both 'sum' and 'numbers.length' are integers, integer division will be performed and the fractional part will be discarded.

