One approach to solve this problem is to use the concept of union find and depth-first search. The steps to solve this problem are to first create a language graph for all users where each user points to all other users who speak the same language. Then, for each group of users who can only speak the same language, find the most common language - this will be the language to teach to the users. In the end, return the total amount of users to teach.

Here is the Python solution for the problem.

```python
from collections import defaultdict
class Solution:
    def minimumTeachings(self, n, languages, friendships):
        languages = list(map(set, languages))
        lang_friends = set()
        common_lang = defaultdict(set)
        parent = list(range(len(languages)))

        def find(x):
            if x != parent[x]:
                parent[x] = find(parent[x])
            return parent[x]

        for u, v in friendships:
            u -= 1
            v -= 1
            if not languages[u] & languages[v]:
                lang_friends.add(u)
                lang_friends.add(v)
                pu, pv = find(u), find(v)
                if pu != pv:
                    parent[pu] = pv

        res, group_size = float('inf'), defaultdict(int)
        for i in map(find, lang_friends):
            group_size[i] += 1
        for user in lang_friends:
            for lang in languages[user]:
                common_lang[(find(user), lang)].add(user)
        for (root, _), users in common_lang.items():
            res = min(res, group_size[root] - len(users))
        return len(lang_friends) if res == float('inf') else res
```
This solution firstly creates friendship graph. For each pair of friends, find out if they share a common language. If not, potentially teach one of them a new language. Use Union-Find to connect these users into groups. Then,scan the language that each friend group's users can speak, and choose to teach the one with the most speakers, hence fewer users need to learn new languages. If there is one group where all users need to learn new languages, return the size of this group.

