Sure, Here is a simple algorithm to print a pyramid pattern in C# 

Below is the algorithm:

```csharp
using System;

class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        Console.Write("Enter the number of rows for the pyramid: ");
        int rows = Convert.ToInt32(Console.ReadLine());

        PrintPyramid(rows);
    }

    static void PrintPyramid(int n)
    {
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
        {
            for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++)
            {
                Console.Write(" "); // Print spaces
            }

            for (int k = 0; k < (2 * i + 1); k++)
            {
                Console.Write("*"); // Print stars
            }

            Console.WriteLine();
        }
    }
}
```

The algorithm starts with printing spaces that decrease in each row and then print the stars which increase for each row. This combination forms a pyramid for a given number of rows.
Here, 'i' is the loop counter to iterate up to the given numbers of 'rows', 'j' is the loop counter to create the leading spaces and 'k' is the loop counter to print the '*' character. 

Just run this console application, provide the number of rows you want for the pyramid when asked, and you get your pyramid.

The function `PrintPyramid(int n)` receives an integer 'n' which denotes the number of rows in the pyramid, and the algorithm runs two loops, the outer one for rows and the inner one for columns. It prints ' ' (space) for the first (n-i-1) columns and '*' for the next (2*i+1) columns. Then it moves to the next line using `Console.WriteLine()`.

