Below is a basic React component for a simple Todo List. This component, called `TodoList`, has a text input where the user can type in a task. When the user presses the "Add Task" button, the task is added to the list below the input.

```jsx
import React, { Component } from 'react';

class TodoList extends Component {
  constructor() {
    super();
    this.state = {
      todos: [],
      currentTodo: ""
    };
  }

  handleChange = event => {
    this.setState({ currentTodo: event.target.value });
  }

  addItem = event => {
    event.preventDefault();
    this.setState({
      currentTodo: "",
      todos: [...this.state.todos, this.state.currentTodo]
    });
  }

  render() {
    return (
      <div className="Todo">
        <h1>Todo List</h1>
        <form onSubmit={this.addItem}>
          <input 
            type="text" 
            name="currentTodo" 
            value={this.state.currentTodo} 
            onChange={this.handleChange} 
          />
          <button type="submit">Add Task</button>
        </form>
        <ul>
          {this.state.todos.map((item, index) => (
            <li key={index}>{item}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    );
  }
}

export default TodoList;
```

This component keeps track of the current value of the input and a list of todos in its state. `handleChange` updates the current input value in the state when the user types in the input field. `addItem` appends the current input value to the list of todos in the state when the user presses the "Add Task" button. The `render` method displays the input field, the "Add Task" button, and a list of todos.

Note that `{this.state.todos.map((item, index) => (<li key={index}>{item}</li>))}` is used to create a new `li` for every todo in the state, displaying all todos on the page.

