我是邀請您進行程式碼重構的批評家。我們的目標是要從程式碼的角度檢討並調整這個函數，使它能計算所提供的整數數組中不重複的整數數量。審視並修正以下編碼方式，確保我們能夠有效率且準確地達成目標。

int count_unique(int array[], int n) 
{ 
    int count = 0; 
    int i; 
    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) { 
        int j; 
        for (j = 0; j < i; j++) { 
            if (array[i] == array[j]) 
                break; 
        } 
        if (i == j) 
            count++; 
    } 
    return count; 
}

output:
The given code is inefficient because it uses a nested loop to traverse the array and check for uniqueness. This results in an O(n^2) time complexity. We can refactor the code by using a set, which is a data structure that only stores unique values. Here is the refactored code:

```c
#include <set> 

int count_unique(int array[], int n) 
{ 
    std::set<int> uniqueElements; 
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) { 
        uniqueElements.insert(array[i]); 
    } 
    return uniqueElements.size(); 
} 
```

This program creates a set and inserts each element of the array into it. When we try to insert a value that's already in the set, it simply gets ignored. Finally, we return the size of the set, which is the number of unique elements in the array.

This program has an O(n log n) time complexity because each insertion into an std::set takes O(log n) time on average and we're performing n insertions.

Sure, the following C++ code calculates the standard deviation of a series of double precision numbers:

```c++
#include <cmath>
#include <vector>
#include <numeric>

double calculateSD(std::vector<double> data){

    double sum = std::accumulate(data.begin(), data.end(), 0.0);
    double mean = sum / data.size();

    double sq_sum = std::inner_product(data.begin(), data.end(), data.begin(), 0.0);
    double stdev = std::sqrt(sq_sum / data.size() - mean * mean);

    return stdev;
}

int main()
{
    std::vector<double> nums = {3.1, 4.6, 7.8, 10.2, 12.4, 14.7, 17.1, 20.3, 22.6, 24.9, 27.0, 29.4, 31.6, 34.0, 36.3};
    std::cout << "Standard Deviation is: " <<  calculateSD(nums) << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```

This code uses the STL function `std::accumulate` to sum up the numbers. `std::inner_product` is used to calculate the sum of squares, and `std::sqrt` to get the square root. The formula used to calculate the standard deviation is the square root of the mean of the squares minus the square of the mean. For the time complexity of this code it's O(n) because we are doing a single pass over the data.

