Here is a Java method named "convertAndReverse" which meets the above requirements. It uses `Character` class methods `toLowerCase()` and `toUpperCase()` to convert the cases of the letters and the `StringBuilder` class method `reverse()` to reverse the order of the words. It splits the entered string into words, processes each word individually, and then combines them in reverse order.

```
public class Main {
   public static void main(String[] args) {
      System.out.println(convertAndReverse("Hello World JAVA ProGrAm"));
   }

   public static String convertAndReverse(String input) {
      String[] words = input.split(" ");
      StringBuilder output = new StringBuilder();

      for (String word : words) {
        StringBuilder temp = new StringBuilder();
        for (char letter : word.toCharArray()) {
            if (Character.isUpperCase(letter)) {
                temp.append(Character.toLowerCase(letter));
            } else {
                temp.append(Character.toUpperCase(letter));
            }
        }
        output.insert(0, temp.toString() + " ");
      }
      // Trim is used to remove the trailing space which may have been added
      return output.toString().trim();
   }
}
```
