This program will give the sum of the largest contiguous sub-array along with the start and the end indices. In case the array contains all negative numbers, it will return the least negative number.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <climits>
using namespace std;

void maxSubArraySum(vector<int> a)
{
    int size = a.size();
    int max_so_far = INT_MIN, max_ending_here = 0,
    start =0, end = 0, s=0;

    for (int i=0; i< size; i++ )
    {
        max_ending_here += a[i];

        if (max_so_far < max_ending_here)
        {
            max_so_far = max_ending_here;
            start = s;
            end = i;
        }

        if (max_ending_here < 0)
        {
            max_ending_here = 0;
            s = i + 1;
        }
    }
    cout << "Maximum contiguous sum is "
        << max_so_far << endl;
    cout << "Starting index "<< start
        << endl << "Ending index "<< end << endl;
}

// Driver code
int main()
{
    vector<int> a = {-2, -3, 4, -1, -2, 1, 5, -3};
    maxSubArraySum(a);
    return 0;
}
```

In this code, the function maxSubArraySum takes a vector of integers as an argument. This function is responsible for calculating the sum of the maximum sub-array and identifying and storing the starting and ending indices. The main function initializes a vector of integers a and calls the function maxSubArraySum with a as an argument.

