In JavaScript, you can use Haversine formula to calculate the circumference of an ellipse. This formula will provide an approximation, not the exact circumference. Here is a simple implementation:

```javascript
const PI = Math.PI;

function findCircumference(semi_major, semi_minor) {
  let h = Math.pow((semi_major - semi_minor), 2) / Math.pow((semi_major + semi_minor), 2);
  let circumference = PI * (semi_major + semi_minor) * (1 + ((3 * h) / (10 + Math.sqrt(4 - 3 * h))));
  return circumference;
}

let semi_major = 5;
let semi_minor = 3;
console.log(findCircumference(semi_major, semi_minor));
```

Please note that this formula provides approximation and will not give a perfect result for a non-circulatory ellipse.

