Here's how to create a function in C++ that accepts an array as an argument and returns the minimum and maximum elements.

First, include the required header file.

```cpp
#include<iostream>
using namespace std;
```

Next, define a function named `findMinMax`. This should accept a pointer to the first element of an array (which can behave like an array itself), and the size of the array. It should return a pair of integers, with the first element being the minimum and the second element the maximum.

```cpp
pair<int, int> findMinMax(int *arr, int size) {
    int min = arr[0];
    int max = arr[0];
    for(int i = 1; i < size; i++) {
        if(arr[i] < min) min = arr[i];
        if(arr[i] > max) max = arr[i];
    }
    return {min, max};
}
```

So with this array you can find the minimum and maximum values.


```cpp
int main() {
    int arr[] = {5, 10, 15, 20, 25};
    int size = sizeof(arr) / sizeof(arr[0]);
    pair<int, int> res = findMinMax(arr, size);
    cout << "Min: " << res.first << ", Max: " << res.second << endl;
    return 0;
}
```

This will print:
```shell
Min: 5, Max: 25
```

This is because it iterates each element in array and maintaining the minimum and maximum value it has seen so far. Finally, it return these values as a pair.

