Here is a simple implementation of sorting an array of strings alphabetically.

This example leans on Java's built-in Arrays.sort method to sort an array of strings, which uses a variation of the QuickSort algorithm. Arrays.sort provides a quick, efficient, built-in way for Java to sort arrays of not only Strings, but entire classes as well.

```java
import java.util.Arrays;

public class SortStringArray {
    public static void main(String args[]) {
        String[] myArray = {"Java", "Python", "C++", "Scala", "JavaScript"};

        //Print unsorted array
