請通過實現互斥鎖，使以下的程式碼達到線程安全。
#include <pthread.h>
int global_int = 0;

void* inc_func(void* arg) {
   global_int++;
   return NULL;
}

int main() {
   pthread thread_a, thread_b;
   ...
   return 0;
}

output:
Here is the same C code but with a mutex lock to ensure thread safety. Mutex (or Mutual Exclusion) is a well-used principle in concurrent programming. Mutex object only allows one thread into a controlled section, implementing the critical section's mutual exclusions concept.

```C
#include <pthread.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int global_int = 0;
pthread_mutex_t lock;

void* inc_func(void* arg) {
   pthread_mutex_lock(&lock); //locking
   global_int++;
   pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock); //unlocking
   return NULL;
}

int main() {
   if (pthread_mutex_init(&lock, NULL) != 0) { 
        printf("\n Mutex initialization failed\n"); 
        return 1; 
    } 

    pthread_t thread_a, thread_b;

    pthread_create(&thread_a, NULL, inc_func, NULL);
    pthread_create(&thread_b, NULL, inc_func, NULL);

    pthread_join(thread_a, NULL);
    pthread_join(thread_b, NULL);

    pthread_mutex_destroy(&lock); //destroying mutex

    printf("Global variable: %d\n", global_int);

    return 0;
}
```

In this program, two threads are created, thread_a and thread_b. Each thread upon its creation executes the function `inc_func`. The function `inc_func` is making modifications to the global variable `global_int`. When one thread executes `inc_func`, it increments `global_int` then releases the lock by `pthread_mutex_unlock()`. This allows the other thread to perform the same task. At the end `pthread_mutex_destroy(&lock)` will destroy the mutex object 'lock'. 

Please, remember that in order to compile code with pthreads flag -pthread should be used: 
```
gcc -pthread filename.c -o filename
```

