For the geometric mean of the same array:

```javascript
function calculateGeometricMean(array) {
    if (!Array.isArray(array) || array.length === 0) {
        console.log('Invalid input!');
        return;
    }
    var product = 1;
    for (var i = 0; i < array.length; i++) {
        if (typeof array[i] !== 'number' || array[i] <= 0) {
            console.log('Invalid input!');
            return;  
        }
        product *= array[i];
    }
    console.log(Math.pow(product, 1 / array.length));
}

calculateGeometricMean([1,2,3,4,5]); // outputs about 2.605
```

This function calculates the geometric mean by multiplying all the elements in the array together, and then raising the product to the power of the reciprocal of the number of elements. It includes error checking similar to that in the corrected arithmetic mean function, and additionally checks that all the array's elements are positive, because the geometric mean is undefined for arrays containing zero or negative values.

