Here I will provide a simple console application written in C# that removes uninterrupted successions of identical characters. This code uses a straightforward concept of string manipulation in C#. 

```csharp
using System;
using System.Text;

namespace RemoveSuccessiveDuplicates
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            string str = "azxxzy";
            StringBuilder newStr = new StringBuilder();

            char lastChar = '\0';
