The arithmetic mean (average) of a set of numbers is the sum of the numbers divided by the count of numbers. The geometric mean of a set is the nth root of the product of the numbers, where n is the count of the numbers. For negative numbers, the geometric mean is undefined, because the nth root of a negative number is a complex number when n is an even integer, and a negative real number when n is an odd integer. So in this solution, I will return Undefined if the array contains a negative number.

Here's a Java-based algorithmic solution:

```java
import java.util.OptionalDouble;
import java.util.stream.IntStream;

public class MeanCalculator {
    private int[] array;

    public MeanCalculator(int[] array) {
        this.array = array;
    }

    public double calculateArithmeticMean() {
        OptionalDouble arithmeticMean = IntStream.of(array).average();
        return arithmeticMean.orElse(Double.NaN);
    }

    public String calculateGeometricMean() {
        int totalProduct = 1;
        for (int number : array) {
            if (number < 0) return "Undefined";
            totalProduct *= number;
        }
        double geometricMean = Math.pow(totalProduct, 1.0 / array.length);
        return String.format("%.2f", geometricMean);
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] array = {4, 7, -11, 15,- 18, 21};
        MeanCalculator meanCalculator = new MeanCalculator(array);
        System.out.println("The arithmetic mean is: " + meanCalculator.calculateArithmeticMean());
        System.out.println("The geometric mean is: " + meanCalculator.calculateGeometricMean());
    }
}
```

In this code, the MeanCalculator class has an instance variable array representing the array of integers. The calculateArithmeticMean method calculates the arithmetic mean (average), and the calculateGeometricMean method calculates the geometrical mean. Note that if the array contains a negative number, the calculateGeometricMean method will returns "Undefined". The main method in the Main class then creates an instance of MeanCalculator and prints the resulting arithmetic and geometric means.

