for (let day = new Date(); day <= lastDayOfCurrentMonth; day.setDate(day.getDate() + 1)) {
    let weekDay = day.getDay();
    if (weekDay !== 0 && weekDay !== 6) {
        businessDays++;
    }
}

console.log(`Last day of the current month: ${lastDayOfCurrentMonth}`);
console.log(`Business days left: ${businessDays}`);
console.log(`Last day of the previous month: ${lastDayOfPreviousMonth}`);
```

This program prints the date and time of the last day of the current month, the number of business days left in the month from the current date, and the last day of the previous month.

Note: JavaScript counts months from 0 (January) to 11 (December), so you have to add 1 to get the correct month for `lastDayOfCurrentMonth` and subtract 1 for `lastDayOfPreviousMonth`.

