在Java語言中，我們可以通過建立一個自定義方法來驗證一個數是否為50到100之間的質數。以下是一個可能的實現方式：

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int num = 67;  // replace with the number you want to check
        if (isPrimeInRange(num)) {
            System.out.println(num + " is a prime number within the range 50 to 100.");
        } else {
            System.out.println(num + " is not a prime number within the range 50 to 100.");
        }
    }

    // method to check if a number is a prime number in the range 50 to 100
    public static boolean isPrimeInRange(int num) {
        if (num < 50 || num > 100) return false;  // out of range
        if (num == 2) return true;  // 2 is a prime number
        if (num % 2 == 0) return false;  // even number is not a prime number
        for (int i = 3; i * i <= num; i += 2) {
            if (num % i == 0) return false;  // can be divided by other number
        }
        return true;  // it's a prime number
    }
}
```

在上述程式碼中，我們首先定義了一個 `num` 變數，你可以把這個變數設定為你要檢查的數字。然後我們使用 `isPrimeInRange(num)` 方法來檢查該數是否為50到100之間的質數。该方法首先檢查數字是否在範圍內，然後檢查其是否為2（2是唯一的偶數質數），最後檢查其是否可以被其他數字整除。如果該數通過所有的檢查，則其為質數。

Here's a Java program that finds the median of two sorted arrays of equal length. This program assumes that both input arrays are already sorted and have same length.

```java
public class MedianOfTwoArrays {
    public static double findMedianSortedArrays(int[] nums1, int[] nums2) {
        int len = nums1.length + nums2.length;
        int[] merged = new int[len];

        int i = 0, j = 0, k = 0;
        while(i < nums1.length && j < nums2.length){
            if(nums1[i] < nums2[j]) {
                merged[k++] = nums1[i++];
            }else {
                merged[k++] = nums2[j++];
            }
        }

        while(i < nums1.length) {
            merged[k++] = nums1[i++];
        }

        while(j < nums2.length){
            merged[k++] = nums2[j++];
        }

        if(len % 2 == 0){
            return (merged[len/2] + merged[len/2 - 1]) / 2.0;
        }else{
            return merged[len/2];
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] nums1 = {1, 2, 3, 4};
        int[] nums2 = {5, 6, 7, 8};
        System.out.println(findMedianSortedArrays(nums1, nums2));
    }
}
```

This Java program first merges the two sorted arrays into one larger sorted array. Then, it checks the length of the merged array to determine whether the length is even or odd. If it is even, the median is the average of the two middle elements. If it is odd, the median is the middle element. This program works for arrays of any equal length.

