        }

        while (!isPrime(oddList.size())) {
            oddList.remove(oddList.size()-1);
        }

        Collections.reverse(oddList);

        System.out.print(oddList);
    }

    public static boolean isPrime(int n){
        if (n <= 1)
            return false;
        for (int i = 2; i < n; i++)
            if (n % i == 0)
                return false;
        return true;
    }
}
```

This program does the following.

- It constructs an Array List (not an array) of Integers with elements of 3, 5, 7, 9.
- It adds each odd number from 11 to 100 to the list.
- If the current number of elements in the list is not a prime number, it removes the last element until a prime number is reached.
- It then reverses the order of elements in the list.
- Finally, the entire list is printed out.

The auxiliary function isPrime checks if a number is prime by dividing it by every number less than itself and checking for remainders.

