The function `getProductofDigits(int n)` uses a while loop to calculate the product of the digits. Inside the loop, `n % 10` gives the last digit in the number, and `n = n / 10;` eliminates the last digit from the number. This process repeats until there's no digit left in the number. 

If you want the program to accept user input, replace `1234` with a Scanner object that can read the user's input.

