In the above case, 'propertyDoesNotExist' is undefined because it was not part of the response object. A simple fix is to handle these errors gracefully:

```typescript
getAboutUsContent(): void {
  this.aboutService.getAboutUsContent()
    .subscribe(
      content => {
        if(content && content.hasOwnProperty('propertyDoesNotExist')){
          console.log(content.propertyDoesNotExist);  
