In Java, you can create a program to find the highest prime number in an array as follows:

```
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] array = {3, 5, 17, 20, 89};
        int maxPrime = 0;

        for (int num : array) {
            if (isPrime(num) && num > maxPrime) {
                maxPrime = num;
            }
        }

        System.out.println(maxPrime);
    }

    private static boolean isPrime(int num) {
        if (num <= 1) {
            return false;
        }
        for (int i = 2; i < num; i++) {
            if (num % i == 0) {
                return false;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```

