Here is a simple Java program to implement a queue using an array:

```java
public class Main
{

    private int capacity;
    int queueArr[];
    int front = 0;
    int rear = -1;
    int currentSize = 0;

    public Main(int queueSize){
        this.capacity = queueSize;
        queueArr = new int[this.capacity];
    }

    public void enqueue(int item) {
        if (isQueueFull()) {
            System.out.println("Overflow ! Unable to add element: "+item);
        } else {
            rear++;
            if(rear == capacity-1){
                rear = 0;
            }
            queueArr[rear] = item;
            currentSize++;
            System.out.println("Element " + item+ " is pushed to Queue !");
        }
    }

    public void dequeue() {
        if (isQueueEmpty()) {
            System.out.println("Underflow ! Unable to remove element from Queue");
        } else {
            front++;
            if(front == capacity-1){
                System.out.println("Pop operation done ! removed: "+queueArr[front-1]);
                front = 0;
            } else {
                System.out.println("Pop operation done ! removed: "+queueArr[front-1]);
            }
            currentSize--;
        }
    }

    public boolean isQueueFull(){
        boolean status = false;
        if (currentSize == capacity){
            status = true;
        }
        return status;
    }

    public boolean isQueueEmpty(){
        boolean status = false;
        if (currentSize == 0){
            status = true;
        }
        return status;
    }

    public static void main(String a[]){

        Main queue = new Main(5);
        queue.enqueue(4);
        queue.dequeue();
        queue.enqueue(56);
        queue.enqueue(2);
        queue.enqueue(67);
        queue.dequeue();
        queue.dequeue();
        queue.enqueue(24);
        queue.dequeue();
        queue.enqueue(98);
        queue.enqueue(45);
        queue.enqueue(23);
        queue.enqueue(435);
    }
}
```

This program creates a queue with a maximum capacity. "enqueue" function is used to insert an element at the rear end and "dequeue" function is used to remove an element from the front. If the queue is already full, then enqueue operation will not work. Similarly, if the queue is empty, then dequeue operation will not work.

