You can create a function in JavaScript which maps each vowel to its successor and replace each vowel in the given string with its successor using the map. Here is a simple solution using the `replace` method and regular expression:

```javascript
function permuteVowels(str) {
    var mapVowels = {
        'a': 'e',
        'e': 'i',
        'i': 'o',
        'o': 'u',
        'u': 'a'
    };

    return str.replace(/[aeiou]/gi, function(match) {
        // 'gi' flag for global and case-insensitive matching
        return mapVowels[match.toLowerCase()];
    });
}

console.log(permuteVowels('hello world')); // 'hillu wurld'
```

In this function, replace takes a regular expression matching any vowel (either case due to the `i` flag) and a function which maps the matched vowel to its successor. The g flag is for global search which means find all matches rather than stopping after the first match. Note that this function also considers uppercase vowels and replace them with their corresponding lowercase successors.

You can modify the function to maintain the case (lower/upper) of the original characters as:

```javascript
function permuteVowels(str) {
    var mapVowels = {
        'a': 'e',
        'e': 'i',
        'i': 'o',
        'o': 'u',
        'u': 'a',
        'A': 'E',
        'E': 'I',
        'I': 'O',
        'O': 'U',
