Here is the Java implementation:

```java
import java.util.LinkedList;
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.ListIterator;

public class LinkedListAverage {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        LinkedList<Integer> values = new LinkedList<>(Arrays.asList(3, 6, 12, 24, 48));
        ListIterator<Integer> iterator = values.listIterator(values.size());

        double sum = 0;
        int count = 0;

        while(iterator.hasPrevious()) {
            int current = iterator.previous();
            sum += current;
            count++;
            System.out.println(current);
        }

        double average = sum / count;
        System.out.println("Average: " + average);
    }
}
```

The above Java program creates a while loop that traverses the provided LinkedList in reverse order using a ListIterator. Inside the loop, it adds each number in the LinkedList to the variable `sum`. The number of elements in the LinkedList is counted by incrementing `count` in each iteration of the loop. After the loop, the average is calculated by dividing sum by count.

