Develop a Java 8 Stream that filters a collection of objects based on specified attributes, taking into consideration the following data set:
[
    {'name': 'John', 'age': 20},
    {'name': 'Smith', 'age': 30},
    {'name': 'Bill', 'age': 40}
]

output:
In Java, data is typically represented by class objects instead of maps or dictionaries like in Python or JavaScript. So, the data set will be represented by a list of `Person` objects. 

Firstly, we need to create a class `Person` to represent the person data:

```java
public class Person {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    public Person(String name, int age) {
        this.name = name;
        this.age = age;
    }

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }

    public int getAge() {
        return age;
    }
}
```

After this we can create a list of `Person` objects and use a Java 8 Stream to filter it:

```java
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<Person> persons = Arrays.asList(
                new Person("John", 20),
                new Person("Smith", 30),
                new Person("Bill", 40));

        // Filter persons older than 20
        List<Person> filteredPersons = persons.stream()
                .filter(person -> person.getAge() > 20)
                .collect(Collectors.toList());

        // Print filtered persons
        filteredPersons.forEach(person -> System.out.println("Name: " + person.getName() + ", Age: " + person.getAge()));
    }
}
```

This program will print out:

Name: Smith, Age: 30
Name: Bill, Age: 40

That's the list of persons older than 20. 

It's important to note Java 8 Stream operations are lazy, it's not executed until it's really needed. This behavior can improve the performance for large data set.

